  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8e0f9034-0a0b-499f-93b9-c87421cf20d6-5b221d5f-a997-41dc-b37b-a0a100bcf37b-9895111.png\" style=\"width: 527px; height: 370px;\" /></p><p>The peptide is having N-terminal at left-hand side and C-terminal at right-hand side. During hydrolysis the bond breaks between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p><p>Hydrolysis of the given tetrapeptide will give the following:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7929ecf0-eb62-4255-be21-0a4c5a305766-9895111_2.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 262px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1f93cdbb-9587-409d-97d3-2ab61f0ec001-9895111_3.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 238px;\" /></p>",
